     +1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234
    0|INSTRUCTIONS FOR MODIFYING PATTERNS                             
    1|                                                                
    2|CREATE PATTERNS AND ANIMATION TABLES USING THE ANIMATION TOOLS  
    3|                                                                
    4|INSERT 'FLOAD' COMMANDS TO LOAD THIS INFORMATION INTO THE       
    5|FILE NAMED 'PAT-LOAD' IF THE CHANGES WOULD MAKE EXISTING        
    6|FILES IN 'PAT-LOAD' OBSELETE, THEN DESTROY THE OBSLETE FILES    
    7|AND REMOVE THE CORRESPONDING 'FLOAD' COMMANDS.                  
    8|                                                                
    9|                                                                
   10|THE FILE NAMED 'ANIM-MAP' CONTAINS INSTRUCTIONS THAT ASSOCIATE  
   11|ANIMATION LISTS AND PATTERNS THAT YOU CREATE WITH               
   12|'INDEX CONSTANTS' DEFINED BY JAY. THE 'INDEX CONSTANTS'         
   13|ARE LISTED IN THE FILE NAMED 'INDEX' WHICH JAY MAINTAINS.       
   14|                                                                
   15|-- MORE --                                                      

BLOCK =   1
     +1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234
    0|AN 'INDEX CONSTANT' IS A SPECIAL NAME THAT JAY'S PROGRAM        
    1|USES TO REFER TO YOUR ANIMATION. BY UPDATING YOUR 'ANIM-MAP'    
    2|FILE YOU FORM THE ASSOCIATION BETWEEN YOUR NAME AND JAY'S NAME. 
    3|THUS YOU CAN CALL YOUR ANIMATIONS AND PATTERNS WHATEVER YOU LIKE
    4|WITHOUT WORRY ABOUT CONFLICTING WITH JAY'S NAME USAGE.          
    5|                                                                
    6|THE FORMAT FOR SPECIFING THIS ASSOCIATION LOOKS LIKE THIS:      
    7|                                                                
    8|<your name> <jays name> AT!                                     
    9|                                                                
   10|THIS EXAMPLE WOULD DEFINE THE PATTERN CALLED 'GORF-PAT' WITH    
   11|THE INDEX CONSTANT 'GORFi':                                     
   12|                                                                
   13|GORF-PAT GORFi AT!                                              
   14|                                                                
   15|-- MORE --                                                      

BLOCK =   2
     +1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234
    0|THE FILE 'ANIM-MAP' CONTAINS A LIST OF LINES LIKE THE           
    1|ONE SHOWN IN THE EXAMPLE. IT IS VERY IMPORTANT THAT THE         
    2|FOLLOWING MISTAKES NOT OCCUR:                                   
    3|                                                                
    4|FORGETING TO ADD A LINE IN THE 'ANIM-MAP' FILE WILL CAUSE       
    5|A UGLY BLOCK TO APPEAR IN THE PLACE OF THE PATTERN YOU WANTED.  
    6|                                                                
    7|DUPLICATE LINES REFERING TO THE SAME INDEX CONSTANT WILL CAUSE  
    8|THE ANIMATION MENTIONED LATER ON TO BE THE ONE USED BY THE      
    9|PROGRAM.                                                        
   10|                                                                
   11|SPELLING MISTAKES WILL CAUSE THE COMPUTER TO PRINT THE MIS-     
   12|SPELLED WORD FOLLOWED BY A QUESTION MARK. TYPING 'WHERE' WILL   
   13|PRINT OUT THE LINE CONTAINING THE MISTAKE. TO CORRECT THIS YOU  
   14|MAY HAVE TO RELOAD FROM THE BEGINING.                           
   15|-- MORE --                                                      

BLOCK =   3
     +1234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234
    0|OTHER MISTAKES YOU MAY MAKE ARE RUNNING OUT OF MEMORY SPACE     
    1|OR OVERFLOWING THE DISK DIRECTORY. IF YOU RUN OUT OF SPACE      
    2|TALK TO JAY ABOUT IT. IF THE DISK DIRECTORY OVERFLOWS           
    3|IT IS RECOMMENDED THAT RELATED OBJECTS BE COMBINED INTO A       
    4|SINGLE FILE. FOR EXAMPLE RATHER THAT HAVING 4 FILES             
    5|EACH CONTAINING ONE PATTERN THEY COULD BE MERGED INTO A         
    6|SINGLE FILE CONTAINING FOUR PATTERN BLOCKS. THIS WILL ALSO      
    7|SAVE CONSIDERABLE TIME WHEN LOADING.                            
